{"success": true, "message": "Test details sent successfully", "data": {"test": {"_id": "69de21eb7e39d99b57bc5aab", "analysisVideoCdn": "yt", "exam": ["605dfcb2f226ac25a8bd5fef"], "ctype": null, "position": 0, "order": 12, "enableCalculator": false, "isContinuousQuestion": false, "reattemptAvailable": false, "singleSectionMultipleSubjects": false, "timeRestricted": false, "title": "Rotational Motion - Test 7", "description": "Previous Year Questions as Chapter Test", "syllabus": "This test contains questions from all topics of this chapter included in the JEE Main syllabus. It includes a mix of questions from PYQs of JEE Main 2019 - 2025.", "totalTime": 40, "totalQuestions": 20, "totalMarks": 80, "bonusQuestions": null, "bonusMarks": null, "startDate": "2026-04-15T03:30:00.000Z", "endDate": "2027-04-30T00:00:00.000Z", "type": "free", "class": "605df635a37b7025c438d685", "instruction": "608289ffb160b022e9442c83", "subjects": [{"subjectId": "607018ee404ae53194e73d90", "totalMarks": 80, "bonusMarks": 0, "totalQuestions": 20, "bonusQuestions": 0, "_id": "69de4f312ee0e063d924db2d"}], "sections": [{"sectionId": {"_id": "69de4f312ee0e063d924db2a", "title": "Physics Numerical", "sectionType": "normal", "subject": "607018ee404ae53194e73d90", "questions": [{"_id": "69de4f312ee0e063d924dab4", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0df82"], "topics": ["60e2fb1f66f9ce3f243b4b5c"], "concepts": ["60e5678c499d1e49588f9259"], "question": {"text": "M and R be the mass and radius of a disc. A small disc of radius $R / 3$ is removed from the bigger disc as shown in figure. The moment of inertia of remaining part of bigger disc about an axis AB passing through the centre O and perpendicular to the plane of disc is $\\frac{4}{x} M R^2$. The value of $x$ is ________.<br/><img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2FKcliJzNaFMnfovgRyc1zuvcly7Fy1k4s-viBpp50uCw.original.fullsize.png?alt=media\"/>"}, "options": [{"id": "fcec21", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f312ee0e063d924dab5"}, {"id": "42a8f9", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f312ee0e063d924dab6"}, {"id": "dae8c0", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f312ee0e063d924dab7"}, {"id": "9ae9c7", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f312ee0e063d924dab8"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f312ee0e063d924dab9", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0df82"], "topics": ["60e40fd6f1ef260f84ed1e9d"], "concepts": ["60e56739499d1e49588f8b55"], "question": {"text": "A thin uniform rod of length <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math>, cross sectional area <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math>&nbsp;and density <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>d</mi></math>&nbsp;is rotated about an axis passing through the centre and perpendicular to its length with angular velocity <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#969;</mi></math>. If value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#969;</mi></math> in terms of its rotational kinetic energy <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>E</mi></math> is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msqrt><mfrac><mrow><mi>&#945;</mi><mi>E</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>A</mi><mi>d</mi></mrow></mfrac></msqrt></math>,&nbsp;then the value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#945;</mi></math>&nbsp;is ______."}, "options": [{"id": "244d5c", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f312ee0e063d924daba"}, {"id": "9a95bb", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f312ee0e063d924dabb"}, {"id": "14f295", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f312ee0e063d924dabc"}, {"id": "279908", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f312ee0e063d924dabd"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f312ee0e063d924dabe", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0df82"], "topics": ["60e2fb5766f9ce3f243b4f40"], "concepts": ["60e2fb5666f9ce3f243b4f0f"], "question": {"text": "If the radius of earth is reduced to three-fourth of its present value without change in its mass then value of duration of the day of earth will be ______ hours 30 minutes."}, "options": [{"id": "c14437", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f312ee0e063d924dabf"}, {"id": "0990fb", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f312ee0e063d924dac0"}, {"id": "a96762", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f312ee0e063d924dac1"}, {"id": "6cfbf6", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f312ee0e063d924dac2"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f312ee0e063d924dac3", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0df82"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b4788"], "concepts": ["60e567dc499d1e49588f9cae"], "question": {"text": "A circular disc reaches from top to bottom of an inclined plane of length <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>L</mi><mo>.</mo></math> When it slips down the plane, it takes time&nbsp;&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math>. When it rolls down the plane, it takes time <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>. The value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mfrac></math> is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msqrt><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mi>x</mi></mfrac></msqrt></math>. The value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi></math> will be"}, "options": [{"id": "7cac75", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f312ee0e063d924dac4"}, {"id": "0c18cd", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f312ee0e063d924dac5"}, {"id": "767cbf", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f312ee0e063d924dac6"}, {"id": "b39887", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f312ee0e063d924dac7"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f312ee0e063d924dac8", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0df82"], "topics": ["60c9e88cea076dc381c0e110"], "concepts": ["6117b76a478ae845c43c6d48"], "question": {"text": "<img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2Fd5a5ba17-736c-4fe6-8d8d-1f8a4eade18a-image.png?alt=media\" style=\"width: 250px; height: 176px;\" /><br /><br />Consider a uniform cubical box of side a on a rough floor that is to be moved by applying minimum possible force <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">F</mi></math> at a point <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">b</mi></math> above its centre of mass (see figure). If the coefficient of friction is <math><mi>&#956;</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.4</mn></math> , the maximum possible value of <math><mn>100</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">b</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi></mrow></mfrac></math> for a box not to topple before moving is ________"}, "options": [{"id": "057a64", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f312ee0e063d924dac9"}, {"id": "0866df", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f312ee0e063d924daca"}, {"id": "74142e", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f312ee0e063d924dacb"}, {"id": "67b24a", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f312ee0e063d924dacc"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f312ee0e063d924dacd", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0df82"], "topics": ["60e2fb1f66f9ce3f243b4b5c"], "concepts": ["6117b88f67dbe2603c3e80a0"], "question": {"text": "The moment of inertia of a uniform thin rod about a perpendicular axis passing through one end is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math>. The same rod is bent into a ring and its moment of inertia&nbsp;about a diameter is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>. If <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mfrac></math> is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mi>x</mi><msup><mi>&#960;</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mn>3</mn></mfrac></math>, then the value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi></math> will be ______."}, "options": [{"id": "46aefd", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f312ee0e063d924dace"}, {"id": "b2aee8", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f312ee0e063d924dacf"}, {"id": "85a637", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f312ee0e063d924dad0"}, {"id": "46d869", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f312ee0e063d924dad1"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f312ee0e063d924dad2", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0df82"], "topics": ["60e40fd6f1ef260f84ed1e9d"], "concepts": ["60e40fd4f1ef260f84ed1e49"], "question": {"text": "A pulley of radius <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math> is rotated about its axis by a force <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>F</mi><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>12</mn><mi>t</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi></math> applied tangentially (while <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>t</mi></math> is measured in seconds). If moment of inertia of the pulley about its axis of rotation is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>kg</mi><msup><mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></math>, the number of rotations made by the pulley before its direction of motion is reversed, will be <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mi>K</mi><mi>&#960;</mi></mfrac></math>. The value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>K</mi></math> is _____ ."}, "options": [{"id": "a99c70", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f312ee0e063d924dad3"}, {"id": "e76016", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f312ee0e063d924dad4"}, {"id": "48dd6b", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f312ee0e063d924dad5"}, {"id": "631053", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f312ee0e063d924dad6"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f312ee0e063d924dad7", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0df82"], "topics": ["60e2fb5766f9ce3f243b4f40"], "concepts": ["60e2fb5666f9ce3f243b4f0f"], "question": {"text": "<p>A thin rod of mass&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>9</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>kg</mi></math> and length&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math> is suspended, at rest, from one end so that it can freely oscillate in the vertical plane. A particle of move&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>kg</mi></math> moving in a straight line with velocity&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>80</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math> hits the rod at its bottom most point and sticks to it (see figure). The angular speed (in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>rad</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>) of the rod immediately after the collision will be &hellip;&hellip;&hellip;&hellip;</p><p><img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2F47cddb2a-1fba-4ea9-897f-c85abb799994-image.png?alt=media\" style=\"width: 148px; height: 145px;\" /></p>"}, "options": [{"id": "033e3b", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f312ee0e063d924dad8"}, {"id": "5ce2ae", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f312ee0e063d924dad9"}, {"id": "4dbbbc", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f312ee0e063d924dada"}, {"id": "3dc09c", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f312ee0e063d924dadb"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f312ee0e063d924dadc", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0df82"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b4788"], "concepts": ["60e567dc499d1e49588f9cae"], "question": {"text": "A solid sphere of mass <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>kg</mi></math> rolls without slipping on a plane surface. Its kinetic energy is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>7</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi></math>. The speed of the centre of mass of the sphere is ______ <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>cm</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>."}, "options": [{"id": "380a34", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f312ee0e063d924dadd"}, {"id": "d96b14", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f312ee0e063d924dade"}, {"id": "23c158", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f312ee0e063d924dadf"}, {"id": "0a0d46", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f312ee0e063d924dae0"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f312ee0e063d924dae1", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0df82"], "topics": ["60e2fb1f66f9ce3f243b4b5c"], "concepts": ["6117b96d67dbe2603c3e9e09"], "question": {"text": "<p>Four particles, each of mass <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo> </mo><mi>kg</mi></math> are placed at four corners of a square of side <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math>. The moment of inertia of the system about an axis perpendicular to its plane and passing through one of its vertex is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>_</mi><mi>_</mi><mi>_</mi><mi>_</mi><mi>_</mi><mi>_</mi><mo> </mo><mi>kg</mi><mo> </mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math>.</p>"}, "options": [{"id": "e01de4", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f312ee0e063d924dae2"}, {"id": "280635", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f312ee0e063d924dae3"}, {"id": "8e289b", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f312ee0e063d924dae4"}, {"id": "ca53c0", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f312ee0e063d924dae5"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f312ee0e063d924dae6", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0df82"], "topics": ["60e40fd6f1ef260f84ed1e9d"], "concepts": ["60e40fd4f1ef260f84ed1e42"], "question": {"text": "A <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>kg</mi></math> steel rod of length <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math> is clamped on a table vertically at its lower end and is free to rotate in the vertical plane. The upper end is pushed so that the rod falls under gravity. Ignoring the friction due to clamping at its lower end, the speed of the free end of the rod when it passes through its lowest position is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>_</mi><mi>_</mi><mi>_</mi><mi>_</mi><mi>_</mi><mi>_</mi><mi>_m</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>.</mo></math><br />(Take <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>g</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn><msup><mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>)</mo></math>"}, "options": [{"id": "9e3841", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f312ee0e063d924dae7"}, {"id": "3792ee", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f312ee0e063d924dae8"}, {"id": "21278b", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f312ee0e063d924dae9"}, {"id": "e09bb3", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f312ee0e063d924daea"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f312ee0e063d924daeb", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0df82"], "topics": ["60e2fb5766f9ce3f243b4f40"], "concepts": ["60e2fb5666f9ce3f243b4f0f"], "question": {"text": "<p>Consider a disc of mass <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn><mo> </mo><mi>kg</mi></math>, radius <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math>, rotating with angular velocity of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>10</mn><mo> </mo><mi>rad</mi><mo> </mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math> about an axis perpendicular to the plane of rotation. An identical disc is kept gently over the rotating disc along the same axis. The energy dissipated so that both the discs continue to rotate together without slipping is _________<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi></math>.</p><img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2Ffd27f85d-47bc-4367-b361-e7a4a9662e25.png?alt=media\" style=\"width: 300px; height: 210px;\"/>"}, "options": [{"id": "7361d4", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f312ee0e063d924daec"}, {"id": "28f826", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f312ee0e063d924daed"}, {"id": "23cebe", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f312ee0e063d924daee"}, {"id": "f21808", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f312ee0e063d924daef"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f312ee0e063d924daf0", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0df82"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b4788"], "concepts": ["60e567dc499d1e49588f9cae"], "question": {"text": "Two bodies, a ring and a solid cylinder of same material are rolling down without slipping an inclined plane. The radii of the bodies are same. The ratio of velocity of the centre of mass at the bottom of the inclined plane of the ring to that of the cylinder is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><msqrt><mi>x</mi></msqrt><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>.</mo></math> Then, the value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi></math> is"}, "options": [{"id": "d6bc7b", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f312ee0e063d924daf1"}, {"id": "81f17d", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f312ee0e063d924daf2"}, {"id": "9e8d82", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f312ee0e063d924daf3"}, {"id": "0147e3", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f312ee0e063d924daf4"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f312ee0e063d924daf5", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0df82"], "topics": ["60e2fb1f66f9ce3f243b4b5c"], "concepts": ["60e567fa499d1e49588fa017"], "question": {"text": "The moment of inertia of a solid disc rotating along its diameter is 2.5 times higher than the moment of inertia of a ring rotating in similar way. The moment of inertia of a solid sphere which has same radius as the disc and rotating in similar way, is $n$ times higher than the moment of inertia of the given ring. Here, $\\mathrm{n}=$_________\nConsider all the bodies have equal masses."}, "options": [{"id": "cd0734", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f312ee0e063d924daf6"}, {"id": "805e09", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f312ee0e063d924daf7"}, {"id": "6c4fb1", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f312ee0e063d924daf8"}, {"id": "fc116a", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f312ee0e063d924daf9"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f312ee0e063d924dafa", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0df82"], "topics": ["60e40fd6f1ef260f84ed1e9d"], "concepts": ["60e5671a499d1e49588f87cd"], "question": {"text": "A person of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>80</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>kg</mi></math> mass is standing on the rim of a circular platform of mass <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>200</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>kg</mi></math> rotating about its axis at&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn></math> revolutions per minute (rpm). The person now starts moving towards the centre of the platform. What will be the rotational speed (in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>rpm</mi></math> ) of the platform when the person reaches its centre...."}, "options": [{"id": "20efbf", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f312ee0e063d924dafb"}, {"id": "179ff7", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f312ee0e063d924dafc"}, {"id": "c5da73", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f312ee0e063d924dafd"}, {"id": "beca70", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f312ee0e063d924dafe"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f312ee0e063d924daff", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0df82"], "topics": ["60e2fb5766f9ce3f243b4f40"], "concepts": ["60e2fb5666f9ce3f243b4f0f"], "question": {"text": "A circular disc of mass <math><mtext>M</mtext></math> and radius <math><mtext>R</mtext></math> is rotating about its axis with angular speed <math><mrow><msub><mi>&#969;</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></math>. If another stationary disc having radius <math><mrow><mfrac><mtext>R</mtext><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow></math> and same mass <math><mtext>M</mtext></math> is dropped co-axially on to the rotating disc. Gradually both discs attain constant angular speed <math><mrow><msub><mi>&#969;</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></math>. The energy lost in the process is <math><mrow><mtext>p%</mtext></mrow></math> of the initial energy. Value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">p</mi></math> is ______"}, "options": [{"id": "8e68c5", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f312ee0e063d924db00"}, {"id": "5cf643", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f312ee0e063d924db01"}, {"id": "857207", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f312ee0e063d924db02"}, {"id": "92daae", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f312ee0e063d924db03"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f312ee0e063d924db04", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0df82"], "topics": ["60e2fb1f66f9ce3f243b4b5c"], "concepts": ["6117b94a67dbe2603c3e992e"], "question": {"text": "A solid sphere and a solid cylinder of same mass and radius are rolling on a horizontal surface without slipping. The ratio of their radius of gyrations respectively <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><msub><mi>k</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mi>p</mi><mi>h</mi></mrow></msub><mo>:</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mrow><mi>c</mi><mi>y</mi><mi>l</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mfenced></math> is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>:</mo><msqrt><mi>x</mi></msqrt></math>. The value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi></math> is _______."}, "options": [{"id": "e989a0", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f312ee0e063d924db05"}, {"id": "58d13f", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f312ee0e063d924db06"}, {"id": "28a3e5", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f312ee0e063d924db07"}, {"id": "488ccb", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f312ee0e063d924db08"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f312ee0e063d924db09", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0df82"], "topics": ["60e40fd6f1ef260f84ed1e9d"], "concepts": ["60e56739499d1e49588f8b55"], "question": {"text": "<p>For rolling spherical shell, the ratio of rotational kinetic energy and total kinetic energy is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mi>x</mi><mn>5</mn></mfrac></math>.&nbsp;The value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi></math> is _____.</p>"}, "options": [{"id": "6064db", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f312ee0e063d924db0a"}, {"id": "8b0e23", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f312ee0e063d924db0b"}, {"id": "fec287", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f312ee0e063d924db0c"}, {"id": "ff6eb2", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f312ee0e063d924db0d"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f312ee0e063d924db0e", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0df82"], "topics": ["60e2fb1f66f9ce3f243b4b5c"], "concepts": ["60e40fd4f1ef260f84ed1e45"], "question": {"text": "<p>Four identical discs each of mass &#39;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>M</mi></math>&#39; and diameter &#39;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>a</mi></math>&#39; are arranged in a small plane as shown in figure. If the moment of inertia of the system about <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>O</mi><msup><mi>O</mi><mo>&#39;</mo></msup></math> is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mi>x</mi><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mi>M</mi><msup><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math>. Then, the value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi></math> will be _____ .</p><p><img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2Fe0a5b2da-c579-4149-aac0-7d0525226316-image.png?alt=media\" style=\"width: 120px; height: 196px;\" /></p>"}, "options": [{"id": "e6b9ba", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f312ee0e063d924db0f"}, {"id": "6da96a", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f312ee0e063d924db10"}, {"id": "45fea9", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f312ee0e063d924db11"}, {"id": "00a9b2", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f312ee0e063d924db12"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f312ee0e063d924db13", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0df82"], "topics": ["60e40fd6f1ef260f84ed1e9d"], "concepts": ["60e5671a499d1e49588f87cd"], "question": {"text": "<p>The angular speed of truck wheel is increased from <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>900</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>rpm</mi></math> to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2460</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>rpm</mi></math> in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>26</mn></math> seconds. The number of revolutions by the truck engine during this time is ______.</p><p>(Assuming the acceleration to be uniform).</p>"}, "options": [{"id": "4de183", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f312ee0e063d924db14"}, {"id": "696c80", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f312ee0e063d924db15"}, {"id": "f4db1d", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f312ee0e063d924db16"}, {"id": "f1c4bc", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f312ee0e063d924db17"}], "questionLabels": []}], "markingScheme": {"_id": "608283c623cf4b3ad8f125e5", "title": "JEE Numerical", "correctAttempt": 4, "incorrectAttempt": -1, "createdAt": "2021-04-09T08:45:27.797Z", "updatedAt": "2021-07-05T05:39:27.056Z", "__v": 0, "updated_by": "6042252509c5bf34e8a2f178"}, "maximumAttemptLimit": 20, "linkedQuestions": [], "createdAt": "2026-04-14T14:29:05.211Z", "updatedAt": "2026-04-14T14:29:05.211Z", "__v": 0}, "position": 0, "_id": "69de4f312ee0e063d924db2c"}], "bonusSections": [], "packDetails": [], "paidFeatures": [], "tags": [], "timeRestrictionSlots": [], "createdAt": "2026-04-14T11:15:55.179Z", "updatedAt": "2026-04-17T04:57:58.577Z", "testType": "PYQs as Chapter Tests", "isResumeBufferAllowed": true, "enableAccessibility": true, "maxAttemptableQuestion": 20, "analysisVideoThumbnail": "", "analysisVideoThumbnailDark": "", "shortTitle": "", "subjectDetails": [{"subjectId": "607018ee404